================================================================================================
B. The three tiling recurrences as Boolean-Mobius kernels
================================================================================================
Letter-level sign packets:
  full B3 A+B+C-D-E-F+G:          +++---+
  even half B2 A+B-C:             ++-
  odd half prompt A+B-C+D-E-F+G:  ++-+--+
  odd half reordered corners A,B,D: +++---+
Readout: odd half has two useful addresses.  In prompt order over
A..G = 1..7 it is chi_7 with the zero/triple slot positive; in corner order A,B,D
it is B3 inclusion-exclusion with pair-overlaps C,E,F.
  chi_7 plus zero/triple slot:       ++-+--+

Pushforward by size/depth offset:
  full staircase:  offsets n-1,n-2,n-3 ->  3, -3, +1
  even half:       offsets n-1,n-2     ->  2, -1
  odd half:        offsets n-1..n-4    ->  2,  0, -2, +1
The zero at n-2 is geometric cancellation (-C + D), not absence of data.

Verification n=5..20: full Delta^3=True, even half=True, odd half=True
Global half recurrence (x-1)^3(x+1): True
Half sequence h_n=floor((n-1)^2/4), n=2..14:
  0, 1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 12, 16, 20, 25, 30, 36, 42

================================================================================================
C. Product-lattice packet bridge
================================================================================================
Independent danger probability x=1/7 through Boolean IE:
  B2 nonempty packet ++-       = 1-(6/7)^2 = 13/49
  B3 nonempty packet +++---+   = 1-(6/7)^3 = 127/343
This is the same Mobius mechanism as phi=mu*id, but on a Boolean
far/tiling lattice instead of a divisor lattice.

Main-term packet sizes for a 13-speed exact-period witness model:
  D=  41: phi(D)=  40, (6/7)^13*phi=  5.3920, B3_packet_capacity=  14.810
  D=  83: phi(D)=  82, (6/7)^13*phi= 11.0536, B3_packet_capacity=  30.362
  D=  89: phi(D)=  88, (6/7)^13*phi= 11.8625, B3_packet_capacity=  32.583
  D= 173: phi(D)= 172, (6/7)^13*phi= 23.1857, B3_packet_capacity=  63.685
  D= 210: phi(D)=  48, (6/7)^13*phi=  6.4704, B3_packet_capacity=  17.773
  D=1260: phi(D)= 288, (6/7)^13*phi= 38.8226, B3_packet_capacity= 106.636
Proof readout: the denominator divisor label and the far/tiling subset
label should live on the product lattice Div(D) x B_r until the residual
error is bounded.  Scalarizing to phi(D) or to a seven-letter sign too
early loses the multiplicativity defect and the geometry of cancellations.

================================================================================================
D. The S109 covering one-tail denominators as coprime packets
================================================================================================
For C={1..11,13}, the q-covering one-tail branch is w=84m and
M=7m/(84m+5).  The witness denominator D=84m+5 is always coprime
to the killed primes 2,3,7, so the proof escapes through unit packets.

  m= 1, D=  89=89            , gcd(D,84)=1, phi/D=88/89, M-1/14=9/1246
